WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:35.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:46.068
THE DREAM LIFE OF MR. KIM

00:00:47.486 --> 00:00:49.821
Sir, are you okay?

00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:52.282
Are you alive?

00:00:55.243 --> 00:00:57.621
Mister.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:00.666
Are you okay?

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.460
Mister? Hey!

00:01:04.503 --> 00:01:06.171
Yes, I'm okay.

00:01:06.254 --> 00:01:07.964
Gosh.

00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:09.341
Jeez.

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:13.011
Damn it, my car is completely wrecked.

00:01:13.804 --> 00:01:15.722
Oh my God. Damn it.

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:19.768
Where the hell is my phone?

00:01:22.396 --> 00:01:23.563
HA-JIN

00:01:23.647 --> 00:01:26.817
You're getting a call
from someone named Ha-jin.

00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:29.403
Give it to me.

00:01:29.486 --> 00:01:30.696
Goodness. Hello?

00:01:30.779 --> 00:01:32.155
Hi, honey.

00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:34.700
Hello, there's been an accident.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.451
Who is this?

00:01:36.535 --> 00:01:39.413
He was driving my car for me.

00:01:39.496 --> 00:01:42.499
Your husband
is my designated driver.

00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:48.588
Honey, it's me.

00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:49.548
Honey.

00:02:52.903 --> 00:02:54.029
Aren't you coming up?

00:02:54.112 --> 00:02:55.530
I am.

00:02:55.614 --> 00:02:58.033
-Then why aren't you getting out?
-I'll be right up.

00:02:59.493 --> 00:03:00.660
Hurry up.

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:23.683
Why is she taking so long?

00:03:26.561 --> 00:03:28.271
Why are you standing there? Go to bed.

00:03:28.355 --> 00:03:29.523
Dad?

00:03:29.606 --> 00:03:30.982
What is it?

00:03:31.942 --> 00:03:34.069
Why are you working
as a designated driver?

00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:36.947
For no reason. Is there a problem?

00:03:37.572 --> 00:03:38.907
I love to drive.

00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:42.494
Is it because of me?

00:03:43.161 --> 00:03:46.081
Don't say things like that.

00:03:46.164 --> 00:03:48.208
Gosh, son.

00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:50.001
You've grown so much.

00:03:50.085 --> 00:03:51.837
When did you get so big?

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:54.506
Mom's here.

00:03:55.048 --> 00:03:57.509
I'm sorry for all the chaos this morning.

00:03:57.592 --> 00:03:59.344
You must not have gotten any sleep.

00:04:00.762 --> 00:04:02.013
Let's go to bed.

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:04.474
Su-gyeom, go to your room.

00:04:14.025 --> 00:04:16.069
Honey, let's just go get some sleep.

00:04:21.825 --> 00:04:22.701
Let's go.

00:04:23.702 --> 00:04:24.578
Where?

00:04:24.661 --> 00:04:25.954
To see a psychiatrist.

00:04:28.164 --> 00:04:29.040
Gosh.

00:04:29.124 --> 00:04:33.044
You heard what the ER doctor said earlier.
Let's just go and hear them out.

00:04:33.128 --> 00:04:35.672
The test results said nothing was wrong.

00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:37.090
Doctors just spout nonsense--

00:04:37.173 --> 00:04:40.260
So you still don't trust doctors?
Fine, I get it.

00:04:41.595 --> 00:04:43.096
Su-gyeom, close the door.

00:04:46.975 --> 00:04:48.351
Then will you listen to me?

00:04:51.897 --> 00:04:54.858
There's so much
that I don't understand right now.

00:04:55.609 --> 00:04:58.236
I don't want to feel like
I'm solving a mystery in my own home.

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.237
It feels horrible.

00:05:00.363 --> 00:05:03.909
So forget what the doctor said
and listen to me.

00:05:05.535 --> 00:05:06.494
Go see a psychiatrist.

00:05:07.871 --> 00:05:09.122
-I'm not going.
-Yes, you are.

00:05:09.205 --> 00:05:11.958
If I say I'm fine, then I'm fine.

00:05:20.175 --> 00:05:22.260
GO STRAIGHT FOR 8 KM

00:05:25.972 --> 00:05:27.015
Hello?

00:05:31.603 --> 00:05:34.189
You son of a bitch.
Why are you so full of yourself?

00:05:34.814 --> 00:05:37.484
Who do you think you are? You egomaniac.

00:05:39.736 --> 00:05:41.154
What are you looking at?

00:05:41.237 --> 00:05:42.656
You should be looking ahead.

00:05:43.615 --> 00:05:44.532
I'm sorry.

00:05:45.742 --> 00:05:47.035
Shut up, you bastard!

00:05:48.328 --> 00:05:51.790
Don't just go through the motions.

00:05:51.873 --> 00:05:54.209
Do some actual work.
Who do you think you are?

00:05:55.418 --> 00:05:57.879
Hey! I said look ahead.

00:05:57.963 --> 00:05:59.547
Rerouting.

00:05:59.631 --> 00:06:00.840
Hang up, you bastard!

00:06:02.258 --> 00:06:05.303
Are you sure this is your destination?
This place is…

00:06:05.887 --> 00:06:08.223
the commercial property I bought.

00:06:08.306 --> 00:06:10.600
Sir, why are we going here?

00:06:14.354 --> 00:06:17.607
So you've buried us
under a mountain of debt

00:06:17.691 --> 00:06:19.359
for the rest of our lives.

00:06:24.906 --> 00:06:26.741
You must have life insurance, right?

00:06:28.284 --> 00:06:29.661
In that case,

00:06:29.744 --> 00:06:31.746
wouldn't this be better?

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.956
What do you think?

00:06:48.972 --> 00:06:50.598
Dad, time for breakfast.

00:06:52.726 --> 00:06:53.601
Dad?

00:06:54.853 --> 00:06:55.812
Dad!

00:06:57.105 --> 00:06:59.441
Mom! Dad is…

00:07:00.025 --> 00:07:00.942
Dad, are you okay?

00:07:01.026 --> 00:07:03.319
-I can't breathe.
-What is it?

00:07:03.403 --> 00:07:04.654
-Honey.
-I can't…

00:07:05.196 --> 00:07:06.489
What's happening?

00:07:07.032 --> 00:07:08.158
-Honey.
-The phone. 911!

00:07:08.241 --> 00:07:10.201
-I can't breathe.
-You can't breathe?

00:07:10.285 --> 00:07:12.704
-I think I need to go to the hospital.
-Okay. Su-gyeom!

00:07:12.787 --> 00:07:13.913
Where did my phone go?

00:07:13.997 --> 00:07:15.081
-To the hospital, now.
-Okay.

00:07:15.165 --> 00:07:17.042
-No.
-Help him up. We'll take him.

00:07:18.084 --> 00:07:19.044
Here we go.

00:07:19.127 --> 00:07:21.004
My God, look at all this sweat.

00:07:21.087 --> 00:07:22.130
-Mom, hold on.
-Okay.

00:07:27.886 --> 00:07:29.971
Hey. Honey.

00:07:32.849 --> 00:07:34.476
I don't think I need to go.

00:07:36.728 --> 00:07:37.604
What?

00:07:37.687 --> 00:07:40.148
I'm feeling better now. Let's go back up.

00:07:40.231 --> 00:07:44.110
You have to go to work.
And you have class soon. Right?

00:07:44.903 --> 00:07:45.779
What?

00:07:45.862 --> 00:07:47.655
I'm fine. Let's go back up.

00:07:50.241 --> 00:07:53.369
Why are you being like this?
I told you I'm fine.

00:07:53.912 --> 00:07:55.830
I'm telling you, I'm perfectly fine.

00:07:59.292 --> 00:08:00.210
Perfectly fine?

00:08:00.293 --> 00:08:04.714
Yes, I just need to get some sleep
and relieve some stress.

00:08:04.798 --> 00:08:06.424
Let's go up.

00:08:06.508 --> 00:08:08.384
Come to your senses, Kim Nak-su!

00:08:09.511 --> 00:08:10.804
Do you think this is normal?

00:08:10.887 --> 00:08:13.431
Is this how a rational person would act?

00:08:13.515 --> 00:08:16.893
What's wrong with you?
Don't you even think about your family?

00:08:17.519 --> 00:08:20.772
You almost died!

00:08:21.648 --> 00:08:23.691
You really need to see a psychiatrist.

00:08:23.775 --> 00:08:27.529
No person in their right mind
would ever act like this.

00:08:27.612 --> 00:08:28.655
Come on.

00:08:29.364 --> 00:08:30.698
Let's go.

00:08:31.241 --> 00:08:32.992
Okay, I'll go.

00:08:33.535 --> 00:08:34.577
-All right.
-Come on.

00:08:35.995 --> 00:08:38.289
No, you stay here.
I'll go with your mom, okay?

00:08:39.082 --> 00:08:40.250
Go to class.

00:08:50.552 --> 00:08:53.096
Why are there so many people here?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.724
PARKING FULL
PLEASE WAIT

00:09:08.862 --> 00:09:10.113
Let's hurry. Come on.

00:09:15.285 --> 00:09:16.953
EUIKANG GENERAL HOSPITAL

00:09:45.231 --> 00:09:46.357
Let's go back to the car.

00:09:46.441 --> 00:09:47.859
What's wrong?

00:09:50.737 --> 00:09:54.407
Look at you. Look at the state you're in.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.867
How have you been--

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.827
Just take me somewhere else. I'm fine.

00:10:00.205 --> 00:10:02.957
Not a general hospital.
Let's go to a clinic with fewer people.

00:10:03.041 --> 00:10:06.127
Why is this place closed today?

00:10:06.211 --> 00:10:07.587
Jeez.

00:10:08.838 --> 00:10:10.340
Stop by the second floor.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.925
We can have a chat.

00:10:12.008 --> 00:10:13.593
Gosh.

00:10:13.676 --> 00:10:15.303
Wait. If that's the case…

00:10:19.182 --> 00:10:21.017
MANGJIN PLAZA

00:10:22.018 --> 00:10:23.019
START NAVIGATION

00:10:23.102 --> 00:10:24.187
Let's go here.

00:10:24.938 --> 00:10:26.231
Do you know this place?

00:10:26.314 --> 00:10:27.690
EPISODE 10
PATIENT IN UNIT 102

00:10:27.774 --> 00:10:29.192
Just drive. Let's go.

00:10:37.033 --> 00:10:39.994
Excuse me, when will the doctor be in?

00:10:40.078 --> 00:10:43.164
I'm not sure.
His schedule is completely open today.

00:10:43.248 --> 00:10:45.291
He must be
taking his time with lunch.

00:10:46.209 --> 00:10:48.461
Please fill out the form first.

00:10:50.713 --> 00:10:52.257
This place doesn't feel right.

00:10:53.007 --> 00:10:54.884
Let's just get it done.

00:10:56.052 --> 00:10:57.303
PANIC DISORDER SYMPTOM CHECKLIST

00:10:57.387 --> 00:10:58.638
…EXPERIENCED ANXIETY OR FEAR?
NO

00:10:58.721 --> 00:11:00.181
ATTACKS START AND PEAK WITHIN MINUTES

00:11:00.265 --> 00:11:01.516
Well, this one…

00:11:01.599 --> 00:11:02.725
NO

00:11:04.936 --> 00:11:07.230
…CHANGED BEHAVIOR TO AVOID ATTACKS
NO

00:11:08.356 --> 00:11:09.732
Answer it honestly.

00:11:09.816 --> 00:11:10.942
I am being honest.

00:11:11.025 --> 00:11:13.403
Nope, and nope.

00:11:13.486 --> 00:11:14.445
I'm back.

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:16.656
Did you have
a five-course meal?

00:11:16.739 --> 00:11:17.782
What took you so long?

00:11:17.865 --> 00:11:19.325
Sangyang Diner went out of business.

00:11:19.409 --> 00:11:20.785
Really?

00:11:20.868 --> 00:11:22.996
So I had to go all the way out there to…

00:11:28.042 --> 00:11:29.919
Look who's here. The owner of--

00:11:30.003 --> 00:11:31.129
Yes, let's go in.

00:11:31.671 --> 00:11:33.006
Doctor, you have to see me.

00:11:33.089 --> 00:11:34.924
Sir, take the form with you.

00:11:35.008 --> 00:11:36.217
Please give it to me.

00:11:38.219 --> 00:11:40.388
-The checklist.
-Right.

00:11:40.471 --> 00:11:42.056
You can go on in now.

00:11:49.188 --> 00:11:50.857
Would you like some tea?

00:11:51.774 --> 00:11:52.859
No, thank you.

00:11:52.942 --> 00:11:55.069
All right. Please have a seat.

00:12:03.536 --> 00:12:05.747
Just for ten minutes, then I'll leave.

00:12:08.624 --> 00:12:10.126
So your wife still doesn't know.

00:12:11.252 --> 00:12:12.128
About what?

00:12:12.211 --> 00:12:14.339
About the first-floor property you bought.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.385
I know what needs to be done.

00:12:19.469 --> 00:12:21.763
Talk it over with her soon
and find a solution together.

00:12:21.846 --> 00:12:23.222
And take your medicine.

00:12:24.098 --> 00:12:25.058
What kind of medicine?

00:12:25.141 --> 00:12:27.185
For your panic disorder, of course.

00:12:27.268 --> 00:12:30.063
I'm prescribing two types.
The first is an anti-anxiety medication.

00:12:30.146 --> 00:12:32.732
Take it when you feel an attack coming
or have trouble breathing.

00:12:32.815 --> 00:12:34.650
The other one is an antidepressant--

00:12:34.734 --> 00:12:35.985
Hey.

00:12:36.611 --> 00:12:38.654
You didn't even look at the checklist.

00:12:38.738 --> 00:12:41.783
You didn't even examine me.
How can you say I have panic disorder?

00:12:41.866 --> 00:12:42.825
What a fraud.

00:12:42.909 --> 00:12:45.161
I've already witnessed
your symptoms myself.

00:12:45.244 --> 00:12:46.496
When?

00:12:48.539 --> 00:12:49.749
Okay.

00:12:51.709 --> 00:12:53.044
Why? What is it?

00:12:53.127 --> 00:12:55.505
Please come over here.

00:12:56.089 --> 00:12:57.215
What's this about?

00:12:59.509 --> 00:13:00.426
All right.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.345
You were walking from over there.

00:13:06.015 --> 00:13:08.393
Then you found it
harder and harder to breathe.

00:13:09.102 --> 00:13:11.813
You clutched your chest and collapsed
right in front of this building,

00:13:11.896 --> 00:13:13.398
Mr. Kim Nak-su.

00:13:16.692 --> 00:13:18.653
I was the one who helped you.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.239
-Are you okay?
-Excuse me.

00:13:21.322 --> 00:13:22.907
I'm a doctor. Please step aside.

00:13:23.825 --> 00:13:24.826
Sir, look at me.

00:13:28.746 --> 00:13:30.498
I want you to breathe into this.

00:13:30.581 --> 00:13:32.208
Take a deep belly breath.

00:13:34.544 --> 00:13:35.545
Keep going.

00:13:38.172 --> 00:13:40.091
Yes, I'm in front of Mangjin Plaza.

00:13:40.633 --> 00:13:42.176
Someone has collapsed here.

00:13:43.886 --> 00:13:45.596
With no patients around,

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:47.557
I'd been staring out the window.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:50.393
I was just doing my job.

00:13:50.476 --> 00:13:52.937
So no need to thank me.

00:13:54.772 --> 00:13:55.773
BOARD CERTIFICATION

00:13:55.857 --> 00:13:57.442
I was ranked second upon admission

00:13:57.525 --> 00:13:58.734
and graduated as valedictorian.

00:13:58.818 --> 00:14:00.361
CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION
PSYCHIATRY

00:14:01.195 --> 00:14:02.655
I didn't ask.

00:14:04.615 --> 00:14:05.825
Anyway.

00:14:06.409 --> 00:14:09.829
I will give you my professional opinion
as a psychiatrist.

00:14:09.912 --> 00:14:11.247
You have panic disorder.

00:14:16.461 --> 00:14:17.837
You have panic disorder.

00:14:20.131 --> 00:14:21.132
Jeez.

00:14:23.217 --> 00:14:24.093
All right.

00:14:25.011 --> 00:14:26.596
Let's call it a condition.

00:14:26.679 --> 00:14:29.223
A cold, stomach flu, muscle aches,

00:14:29.307 --> 00:14:31.559
and panic disorder. It's just a condition.

00:14:33.603 --> 00:14:35.313
So I just have to change my mindset,

00:14:35.396 --> 00:14:37.857
think positive, go stay at a temple,

00:14:38.357 --> 00:14:39.650
work out, and I'll get better?

00:14:39.734 --> 00:14:42.487
No, it cannot be cured
by willpower alone.

00:14:43.196 --> 00:14:45.114
Then what am I supposed to do
to get better?

00:14:46.491 --> 00:14:48.743
Well, let's take our time
and have a cup of tea.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.037
Is it a cure for panic disorder?

00:14:52.288 --> 00:14:53.414
No, there's no such thing.

00:14:53.498 --> 00:14:54.624
Then I won't have any.

00:14:57.835 --> 00:14:58.753
Okay.

00:14:59.253 --> 00:15:02.840
Medication, cognitive behavioral therapy,
and breathing exercises.

00:15:02.924 --> 00:15:05.384
Panic disorder treatment
should be approached step-by--

00:15:05.468 --> 00:15:07.220
I don't have time for that right now.

00:15:07.303 --> 00:15:08.554
You know that.

00:15:08.638 --> 00:15:10.306
I have to manage that damn unit.

00:15:10.389 --> 00:15:12.767
I don't have the luxury
to do that right now.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.478
-What kind of managing are you doing?
-I have to clean it every day

00:15:15.561 --> 00:15:17.605
to get it ready for potential tenants.

00:15:17.688 --> 00:15:20.358
If you slap on a sign that says
"first three months free,"

00:15:20.441 --> 00:15:22.318
do you think a tenant will just show up?

00:15:25.655 --> 00:15:27.907
Then why did you move in here?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.909
Just how much is the rent?

00:15:32.912 --> 00:15:34.622
-I don't pay rent.
-What?

00:15:35.456 --> 00:15:38.042
Weren't you tempted by the promise
of a franchise cafe moving in?

00:15:38.125 --> 00:15:40.461
-Yes.
-"A commercial area like Gangnam Station."

00:15:40.545 --> 00:15:44.549
"A three-minute walk from the station."
"The director will cut you a great deal."

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.426
-Right.
-And when you said yes,

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:49.929
he told you to discuss it
with your family and come back.

00:15:50.012 --> 00:15:50.930
Yes.

00:15:51.013 --> 00:15:53.224
Those slick tablet taps
and speedy calculator moves

00:15:53.307 --> 00:15:55.560
probably mesmerized you.

00:15:56.185 --> 00:15:57.478
Don't tell me you…

00:15:58.813 --> 00:15:59.814
Yes.

00:16:02.525 --> 00:16:05.861
I was also one of the first people
to buy a unit in this building.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.115
Damn it.

00:16:10.908 --> 00:16:11.909
Jeez.

00:16:16.622 --> 00:16:17.915
Let's go.

00:16:17.999 --> 00:16:19.125
Hurry.

00:16:19.208 --> 00:16:20.543
Excuse me. I need to pay.

00:16:20.626 --> 00:16:22.169
Please get your prescription too.

00:16:22.253 --> 00:16:23.129
-Okay.
-All right.

00:16:29.135 --> 00:16:30.011
MANGJIN PLAZA

00:16:30.845 --> 00:16:32.555
You insisted on coming to this clinic.

00:16:32.638 --> 00:16:33.723
What's wrong?

00:16:33.806 --> 00:16:34.807
Look, honey.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.602
A doctor should at least be
smarter than me, right?

00:16:37.685 --> 00:16:40.062
-Yes.
-So I can trust him with my treatment.

00:16:40.146 --> 00:16:41.355
And?

00:16:42.023 --> 00:16:44.275
I think we're on
the same level of stupidity.

00:16:44.358 --> 00:16:45.401
I can't trust that guy.

00:16:46.068 --> 00:16:48.696
What on earth did you two talk about?

00:16:48.779 --> 00:16:50.156
Sir!

00:16:50.239 --> 00:16:51.115
Sir!

00:16:52.325 --> 00:16:55.202
-Sir!
-Gosh, let's go.

00:16:55.286 --> 00:16:57.788
-Is she calling you? She's--
-Where are you going?

00:16:57.872 --> 00:16:59.290
Why haven't you answered my calls?

00:16:59.373 --> 00:17:00.916
I think you have the wrong person.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.003
I finally got a call.
Someone wants to see it tomorrow.

00:17:04.086 --> 00:17:05.713
-Well…
-What do you say?

00:17:05.796 --> 00:17:06.881
It's just…

00:17:06.964 --> 00:17:09.216
Now I remember.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.969
I actually quit ACT.

00:17:12.053 --> 00:17:14.472
She's the CEO of a former client.

00:17:14.555 --> 00:17:16.891
-She must not know I quit.
-What are you talking about?

00:17:16.974 --> 00:17:18.684
Someone's coming to see Unit 102.

00:17:20.603 --> 00:17:21.604
Unit 102?

00:17:21.687 --> 00:17:23.814
You must be his wife.

00:17:23.898 --> 00:17:25.650
You've been so worried, haven't you?

00:17:26.275 --> 00:17:28.486
You should be nice to her
after everything--

00:17:29.028 --> 00:17:30.488
What?

00:17:31.113 --> 00:17:32.615
I see.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.533
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:17:38.788 --> 00:17:40.414
Three months' rent free, right?

00:17:40.498 --> 00:17:41.540
Yes, right.

00:17:45.544 --> 00:17:47.004
FOR LEASE
THREE MILLION WON PER MONTH

00:17:47.088 --> 00:17:49.799
FIRST THREE MONTHS FREE!
RESTAURANTS, CAFES, SELF-CHECKOUT STORES

00:18:16.492 --> 00:18:17.827
Did you buy this?

00:18:23.666 --> 00:18:24.917
How much was it?

00:18:28.796 --> 00:18:29.964
One billion

00:18:31.048 --> 00:18:31.924
fifty million won.

00:18:35.094 --> 00:18:36.053
Wait.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.350
Where did you get that money?

00:18:43.561 --> 00:18:47.148
I took out a loan for 550 million won.

00:18:48.816 --> 00:18:49.942
And?

00:18:50.568 --> 00:18:51.777
The other 500 million…

00:18:56.782 --> 00:18:57.950
was my severance pay.

00:19:01.746 --> 00:19:02.788
Severance…

00:19:02.872 --> 00:19:05.541
It's our 1.05 billion-won property.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.502
I'll work hard. I'm sorry.

00:19:08.586 --> 00:19:09.879
Kim Nak-su.

00:19:09.962 --> 00:19:12.423
I was going to tell you,
but I didn't get a chance.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.300
Kim Nak-su!

00:19:15.384 --> 00:19:17.011
-Kim Nak-su.
-I'm sorry.

00:19:17.094 --> 00:19:18.596
Come on, Kim Nak-su.

00:19:18.679 --> 00:19:20.222
Kim Nak-su.

00:19:20.723 --> 00:19:22.141
Kim Nak-su!

00:19:22.224 --> 00:19:24.435
Kim Nak-su!

00:19:24.518 --> 00:19:27.313
Kim Nak-su!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.487
I'm sorry.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.697
Kim Nak-su!

00:19:38.324 --> 00:19:40.743
Face reality and tell your loved ones.

00:19:42.036 --> 00:19:43.120
Good.

00:19:44.288 --> 00:19:46.165
You're doing great.

00:19:47.958 --> 00:19:49.960
3,208,333 WON

00:20:00.429 --> 00:20:01.847
Give me one.

00:20:03.766 --> 00:20:04.809
Come on.

00:20:04.892 --> 00:20:07.144
I quit 20 years ago, after I had Su-gyeom.

00:20:07.228 --> 00:20:08.854
But I'm craving one like crazy right now.

00:20:08.938 --> 00:20:10.272
Give me one now.

00:20:11.315 --> 00:20:13.442
I'm sorry. Please don't.

00:20:19.114 --> 00:20:20.241
What about the stocks?

00:20:22.409 --> 00:20:23.452
I sold them.

00:20:23.536 --> 00:20:25.412
Both US and domestic?

00:20:32.169 --> 00:20:33.379
Where did that money go?

00:20:39.802 --> 00:20:41.804
MOM

00:20:44.348 --> 00:20:47.184
517 DONGCHEON-DAERO, SINPYEONG-SI
GYEONGGI-DO, MANGJIN PLAZA

00:20:49.144 --> 00:20:51.730
Keep going straight, then left.
Hey, Su-gyeom.

00:20:52.273 --> 00:20:54.066
Over here.

00:20:57.611 --> 00:20:58.988
What is this place, Dad?

00:21:08.455 --> 00:21:09.874
Su-gyeom is here.

00:21:18.048 --> 00:21:18.924
Kim Su-gyeom.

00:21:19.008 --> 00:21:20.259
Yes?

00:21:20.342 --> 00:21:24.263
Did the CEO of your company take out
a 30 million won loan under your name?

00:21:29.935 --> 00:21:30.853
Is that true?

00:21:35.524 --> 00:21:36.400
Yes.

00:21:36.483 --> 00:21:38.360
So to pay that back,

00:21:38.444 --> 00:21:41.196
you were running a business
with the money Dad gave you?

00:21:42.031 --> 00:21:43.198
Yes.

00:21:50.664 --> 00:21:52.207
-Okay.
-Where are you going?

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.173
Do you two even consider me
part of this family?

00:21:59.798 --> 00:22:00.674
Of course.

00:22:00.758 --> 00:22:03.802
Then how could you
move all that money around without…

00:22:04.762 --> 00:22:06.513
Without even talking to me once?

00:22:08.182 --> 00:22:10.726
And what do you expect me
to do about it now?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:15.898
I don't know.

00:22:16.607 --> 00:22:18.192
I don't know anything anymore.

00:22:19.944 --> 00:22:21.278
Where…

00:22:22.696 --> 00:22:23.614
Honey.

00:22:24.657 --> 00:22:27.576
Dad, what is going on?

00:22:28.494 --> 00:22:31.330
How did things get this bad?

00:22:33.332 --> 00:22:35.084
And what is this place?

00:22:46.220 --> 00:22:47.680
We can't go home for a while.

00:23:08.993 --> 00:23:10.619
Loafer. Where are you?

00:23:11.495 --> 00:23:12.371
A trip?

00:23:12.871 --> 00:23:14.331
So is your place empty?

00:23:15.165 --> 00:23:16.750
Your daughter didn't go with you?

00:23:16.834 --> 00:23:19.712
Hey, didn't you say
the third floor was vacant?

00:23:20.337 --> 00:23:23.007
Could Su-gyeom and I
maybe crash there for tonight?

00:23:24.091 --> 00:23:25.092
It's taken?

00:23:25.634 --> 00:23:28.303
Man, maybe it's the location.
Your building is never vacant.

00:23:28.387 --> 00:23:30.097
All right. Have a great time.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.181
Okay.

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:35.644
Jeez.

00:23:37.229 --> 00:23:39.314
Let's go to a 24-hour sauna.

00:23:39.857 --> 00:23:41.692
And make plans there.

00:23:42.943 --> 00:23:44.111
Let's go.

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:50.367
Hey.

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:53.996
Are you mad at me right now
for telling your mom?

00:23:55.998 --> 00:23:57.916
What was I supposed to do?

00:23:58.584 --> 00:24:01.378
She grilled me like a tax auditor.

00:24:01.462 --> 00:24:03.380
I had to come clean.

00:24:03.464 --> 00:24:04.673
Get up. Let's go.

00:24:07.509 --> 00:24:09.678
I really don't understand you.

00:24:11.013 --> 00:24:12.306
What do you mean?

00:24:21.648 --> 00:24:22.983
Did you

00:24:24.443 --> 00:24:28.322
really invest in this for Mom and me?

00:24:29.615 --> 00:24:30.783
Good lord.

00:24:36.955 --> 00:24:38.916
You wanted to show off, didn't you?

00:24:40.459 --> 00:24:43.087
"Even though I got pushed out of my job,
I'm still doing well."

00:24:43.170 --> 00:24:44.880
You had something to prove.

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.757
Right, Dad?

00:24:49.134 --> 00:24:51.470
That's enough. Stop.

00:24:52.137 --> 00:24:53.472
You rascal.

00:24:57.559 --> 00:25:01.396
It was the same
when you made me retake my CSAT.

00:25:02.481 --> 00:25:05.734
You said it was all for me,
but in the end…

00:25:07.486 --> 00:25:09.196
you wanted to be the father

00:25:10.155 --> 00:25:12.491
of a son who went to
Seoul National University.

00:25:12.574 --> 00:25:13.867
Am I wrong?

00:25:16.662 --> 00:25:18.413
You little brat.

00:25:18.497 --> 00:25:20.916
What the family really wants,

00:25:21.583 --> 00:25:23.418
what we're all worried about…

00:25:26.130 --> 00:25:27.881
you don't even know or care.

00:25:29.883 --> 00:25:33.178
Seoul National University, this building…

00:25:37.850 --> 00:25:39.768
That's not what we wanted, Dad.

00:26:20.142 --> 00:26:23.187
You'll worry. "What if I die?
What if this happens again?"

00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:25.856
So you become sensitive
to the slightest changes in your body.

00:26:25.939 --> 00:26:29.568
If your heart beats a little faster
or you're a bit short of breath,

00:26:29.651 --> 00:26:30.569
you wonder…

00:26:41.747 --> 00:26:44.541
Ma'am, since this is a corner spot,

00:26:44.625 --> 00:26:46.168
you'll get all the people passing by.

00:26:46.251 --> 00:26:48.128
And from this way too.

00:26:48.212 --> 00:26:50.130
Take your time and look around.

00:26:51.882 --> 00:26:54.593
This place has been vacant
since it was first sold, right?

00:26:54.676 --> 00:26:55.552
Yes, but--

00:26:55.636 --> 00:26:57.262
Someone who truly sees its value

00:26:57.346 --> 00:26:58.680
hasn't come along yet.

00:27:00.849 --> 00:27:02.059
Right.

00:27:02.142 --> 00:27:03.602
Thank you for showing me around.

00:27:03.685 --> 00:27:06.438
Yes, take care.
I'll be waiting for your wise decision.

00:27:06.521 --> 00:27:07.564
Please give us a call.

00:27:07.648 --> 00:27:10.025
Please wait here
for a moment. Don't go.

00:27:14.613 --> 00:27:17.824
Did I say something I shouldn't have
in front of your wife?

00:27:17.908 --> 00:27:19.159
No, it's fine.

00:27:19.243 --> 00:27:21.328
You're looking so run-down lately.

00:27:21.411 --> 00:27:23.372
Wipe the sleep out of your eyes

00:27:23.455 --> 00:27:24.414
and shave.

00:27:24.498 --> 00:27:26.458
I will. I'm counting on you--

00:27:26.541 --> 00:27:27.417
Okay.

00:27:27.501 --> 00:27:29.753
-Goodness gracious.
-Please call me.

00:27:29.836 --> 00:27:30.879
All right, I will.

00:27:32.005 --> 00:27:34.049
Ma'am, don't just leave like that.

00:27:34.132 --> 00:27:36.093
I have other places to show you.

00:27:45.602 --> 00:27:46.645
Jeez.

00:27:54.903 --> 00:27:55.988
Gosh.

00:27:58.949 --> 00:27:59.825
What?

00:28:04.246 --> 00:28:05.372
What the heck?

00:28:09.251 --> 00:28:10.335
Shoot.

00:28:11.461 --> 00:28:12.754
Damn it.

00:28:15.632 --> 00:28:16.842
Did you sleep here again?

00:28:20.262 --> 00:28:22.597
-What the…
-The water's not working.

00:28:23.348 --> 00:28:25.309
Man, this building is hopeless.

00:28:25.392 --> 00:28:27.561
Excuse me, Dr. Na.

00:28:30.188 --> 00:28:32.357
I was rude to you yesterday.

00:28:34.067 --> 00:28:35.319
Sir.

00:28:35.986 --> 00:28:38.071
Can you help me with this?

00:28:40.782 --> 00:28:42.075
My eyes are burning.

00:28:43.535 --> 00:28:44.411
Dr. Na.

00:28:46.413 --> 00:28:47.706
That's so refreshing.

00:28:48.874 --> 00:28:50.292
That could've been bad.

00:28:50.917 --> 00:28:53.712
Thanks to you,
I'm all cleaned up.

00:28:56.048 --> 00:28:58.508
Talking to your wife made you feel

00:28:59.092 --> 00:29:00.594
a bit better, didn't it?

00:29:02.137 --> 00:29:03.221
How did you know?

00:29:03.305 --> 00:29:04.389
It wasn't on purpose.

00:29:05.515 --> 00:29:07.142
I kept hearing voices from outside.

00:29:07.225 --> 00:29:08.977
What a terrible hobby you have.

00:29:10.729 --> 00:29:14.358
Do you remember when you first felt
symptoms of a panic attack?

00:29:18.195 --> 00:29:20.322
You could have a very serious accident.

00:29:22.449 --> 00:29:23.784
No one dies from a panic attack.

00:29:23.867 --> 00:29:24.868
But

00:29:25.410 --> 00:29:27.079
what if a sudden panic attack hits

00:29:27.746 --> 00:29:29.790
in a truly dangerous moment?

00:29:29.873 --> 00:29:31.541
Damn it.

00:29:31.625 --> 00:29:33.502
I said to swear at him!

00:29:33.585 --> 00:29:34.586
Swear!

00:29:34.669 --> 00:29:35.796
Hey!

00:29:37.756 --> 00:29:39.049
CONSTRUCTION AHEAD
REDUCE SPEED

00:29:40.717 --> 00:29:43.053
Your whole life
could vanish in an instant.

00:29:49.017 --> 00:29:49.893
Well,

00:29:51.061 --> 00:29:53.063
I keep work matters to myself,
even with my wife.

00:29:53.146 --> 00:29:56.233
Let alone my son. And…

00:29:56.858 --> 00:29:58.568
God.

00:29:58.652 --> 00:30:01.530
Sitting face-to-face
with a complete stranger,

00:30:01.613 --> 00:30:04.991
talking about myself,
and going to counseling…

00:30:05.075 --> 00:30:06.701
I really can't do that.

00:30:06.785 --> 00:30:08.453
If it's too difficult…

00:30:10.539 --> 00:30:12.416
why don't we do it

00:30:14.042 --> 00:30:15.252
in a different location?

00:30:19.089 --> 00:30:20.382
DR. NA DAE-RYONG

00:30:24.845 --> 00:30:26.138
Aren't you coming back?

00:30:26.221 --> 00:30:27.431
I'm with a patient.

00:30:32.936 --> 00:30:33.979
And?

00:30:48.535 --> 00:30:49.703
Anyway…

00:30:52.122 --> 00:30:56.793
So he and I…
joined the company at the same time.

00:30:58.170 --> 00:31:01.840
That guy had been a manager forever,

00:31:02.424 --> 00:31:03.842
and then the company

00:31:05.051 --> 00:31:07.179
suddenly sent him to Ulleungdo.

00:31:08.930 --> 00:31:10.265
A few days later,

00:31:10.849 --> 00:31:14.436
he lit charcoal briquettes inside his car
in the company's parking lot.

00:31:17.063 --> 00:31:18.273
So that's why.

00:31:18.356 --> 00:31:22.319
Ever since then, whenever
something bad happened at work,

00:31:23.862 --> 00:31:26.114
I'd find it hard to breathe.

00:31:26.198 --> 00:31:29.201
And my chest would feel
like it was being crushed.

00:31:29.284 --> 00:31:30.535
That's how it was.

00:31:31.411 --> 00:31:32.412
I see.

00:31:35.874 --> 00:31:37.542
The way things work

00:31:38.502 --> 00:31:43.423
in a major corporation
can be frustrating, you know?

00:31:43.507 --> 00:31:45.342
There's pressure from the top

00:31:45.425 --> 00:31:47.636
and from juniors
trying to climb the ladder.

00:31:47.719 --> 00:31:48.637
God.

00:31:50.222 --> 00:31:53.350
I'm sure you wouldn't understand it.

00:31:55.644 --> 00:31:56.520
Mr. Kim.

00:31:57.062 --> 00:31:59.856
I worked at a university hospital.

00:32:00.565 --> 00:32:01.816
And?

00:32:02.609 --> 00:32:05.070
Factions, connections, politics.

00:32:06.655 --> 00:32:07.948
It's the same there too.

00:32:09.491 --> 00:32:12.661
Right. I've seen it on TV.

00:32:13.203 --> 00:32:15.705
Is it really that bad there too?

00:32:19.209 --> 00:32:20.460
Is it?

00:32:21.586 --> 00:32:23.380
Let's not talk about me. Anyway…

00:32:23.463 --> 00:32:24.506
Please, tell me.

00:32:24.589 --> 00:32:26.258
Why did you leave?

00:32:26.341 --> 00:32:27.509
Well?

00:32:28.134 --> 00:32:32.222
Perhaps you were betrayed
by a senior you trusted?

00:32:32.305 --> 00:32:33.431
Were you?

00:32:34.474 --> 00:32:36.268
Okay, that's enough.

00:32:36.351 --> 00:32:38.395
Now tell me about you.

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:47.195
I really thought of my mentor

00:32:48.280 --> 00:32:52.951
as more of a brother
than my own older brother.

00:32:53.034 --> 00:32:54.869
For 25 long years…

00:32:57.872 --> 00:33:00.125
From what you've said,

00:33:00.667 --> 00:33:04.546
getting scammed on the commercial building
was just the final straw.

00:33:04.629 --> 00:33:07.299
Even back at the company,
things were already festering badly.

00:33:07.382 --> 00:33:09.134
Your mental state, I mean.

00:33:09.676 --> 00:33:10.844
People in South Korea

00:33:10.927 --> 00:33:14.389
feel the most stress at their workplace.

00:33:14.889 --> 00:33:17.934
After going through the school system
and university entrance exams,

00:33:18.018 --> 00:33:20.145
the competitive DNA
that's been ingrained in us

00:33:20.228 --> 00:33:22.731
fully blossoms at work.

00:33:23.315 --> 00:33:25.900
Competition never stressed me out.

00:33:27.986 --> 00:33:30.947
Of course, there are some who say that.

00:33:31.489 --> 00:33:32.741
No, I'm serious.

00:33:32.824 --> 00:33:35.368
Competition was just part of life
even when I was a kid.

00:33:36.411 --> 00:33:39.372
I was already competing
with my older brother at home.

00:33:40.749 --> 00:33:42.334
What did you compete with him over?

00:33:42.417 --> 00:33:43.460
Our grades, of course.

00:33:44.377 --> 00:33:45.629
Was your brother a good student?

00:33:45.712 --> 00:33:48.048
Please. He was always at the top.

00:33:48.131 --> 00:33:50.759
Class president, student body president.
He was no joke.

00:33:50.842 --> 00:33:53.720
As the eldest son,
he must have already been the favorite.

00:33:53.803 --> 00:33:57.807
And since he was a good student,
he must've been the family's top priority.

00:33:57.891 --> 00:34:00.727
My parents subtly encouraged competition.

00:34:01.478 --> 00:34:04.773
"If you want to be acknowledged
like your brother,

00:34:04.856 --> 00:34:06.441
do something worthwhile."

00:34:06.524 --> 00:34:09.569
So, did your brother end up going
to a better college than you?

00:34:09.653 --> 00:34:10.695
No.

00:34:11.237 --> 00:34:12.238
After his third try,

00:34:12.322 --> 00:34:14.491
he ended up
at a private university out of town.

00:34:14.574 --> 00:34:17.452
And I got a better job than he did.

00:34:20.830 --> 00:34:22.290
So you won.

00:34:24.876 --> 00:34:26.586
And at that moment,

00:34:27.253 --> 00:34:28.380
how did you feel?

00:34:37.514 --> 00:34:39.057
Let's stop here for today.

00:34:46.272 --> 00:34:47.857
That's the last one, right?

00:34:47.941 --> 00:34:48.942
Yes.

00:34:50.652 --> 00:34:52.445
There's still so much left.

00:34:53.822 --> 00:34:56.825
Sorry. I'll find another place soon.

00:34:59.953 --> 00:35:03.748
What's all that stuff back there?
Did you draw them?

00:35:06.292 --> 00:35:08.878
The roommate I'm living with
is an art major.

00:35:08.962 --> 00:35:12.090
I just kind of dabble on the side.

00:35:13.550 --> 00:35:15.009
Can I take a quick look?

00:35:15.093 --> 00:35:16.177
Sure.

00:35:24.269 --> 00:35:25.270
Wow.

00:35:28.440 --> 00:35:30.442
Which ones are yours?

00:35:30.525 --> 00:35:34.946
This one, and…
I painted everything here.

00:35:40.326 --> 00:35:42.370
Han-na, this is way beyond a hobby.

00:35:43.663 --> 00:35:45.206
-Do you think so?
-Yes.

00:35:45.290 --> 00:35:48.209
There's…
there's something special about these.

00:35:49.669 --> 00:35:50.545
Something special?

00:35:51.838 --> 00:35:53.089
Is there?

00:36:01.055 --> 00:36:03.433
Han-na, should we put something like this

00:36:04.684 --> 00:36:05.769
on our hoodies?

00:36:07.687 --> 00:36:09.063
-This?
-Yes.

00:36:09.731 --> 00:36:11.232
No way. It's too embarrassing.

00:36:11.775 --> 00:36:13.359
They're not good enough to sell.

00:36:13.443 --> 00:36:14.611
That's not true.

00:36:15.737 --> 00:36:18.031
Come on. They're so much better than this.

00:36:20.283 --> 00:36:21.284
I guess you're right.

00:36:28.833 --> 00:36:30.877
Did you ever think of majoring in art?

00:36:30.960 --> 00:36:34.130
I did. I used to love drawing.

00:36:34.214 --> 00:36:36.049
I even applied to design schools.

00:36:36.674 --> 00:36:38.134
I got into a few.

00:36:39.385 --> 00:36:40.261
I see.

00:36:41.054 --> 00:36:41.930
And?

00:36:42.013 --> 00:36:44.974
My father wanted me
to take a gap year and retake the SAT.

00:36:45.058 --> 00:36:48.019
So I ended up at Michigan Tech,
which was never in my plans.

00:36:48.102 --> 00:36:49.604
You know how it is.

00:36:52.524 --> 00:36:54.651
Why are parents like that?

00:36:54.734 --> 00:36:56.569
The problem is how they go about it.

00:36:58.822 --> 00:37:01.282
I still think it's a form of love.

00:37:02.116 --> 00:37:04.244
Because that's probably how they grew up,

00:37:05.370 --> 00:37:08.206
and that's the only way
they know how to express themselves.

00:37:24.472 --> 00:37:26.808
Yes, three samples for now.

00:37:32.730 --> 00:37:36.025
Okay, I'll see you then. Thank you.

00:37:39.904 --> 00:37:41.072
They said to come next week.

00:37:42.699 --> 00:37:45.785
You have some serious drive.

00:37:48.621 --> 00:37:49.539
I'm heading out.

00:37:50.498 --> 00:37:53.042
Where are you going to sleep tonight?

00:37:55.503 --> 00:37:57.922
I was planning to go to a 24-hour sauna.

00:37:58.590 --> 00:38:00.133
Internet cafes are just…

00:38:02.635 --> 00:38:03.761
Do you want to sleep here?

00:38:07.765 --> 00:38:08.725
What?

00:38:09.684 --> 00:38:10.643
Damn it.

00:38:12.228 --> 00:38:14.355
-Sir.
-What? Is it urgent?

00:38:14.439 --> 00:38:15.398
No, it's not.

00:38:15.481 --> 00:38:17.108
Someone's here to see you.

00:38:18.067 --> 00:38:19.193
Jeez.

00:38:20.737 --> 00:38:22.363
CAR MAINTENANCE FROM A TO Z

00:38:22.447 --> 00:38:23.531
Who?

00:38:24.157 --> 00:38:25.366
That guy.

00:38:28.161 --> 00:38:29.621
-Get back to work.
-Yes, sir.

00:38:31.164 --> 00:38:32.332
Ho-jun.

00:38:40.256 --> 00:38:41.925
Managing Director Kim Nak-su.

00:38:47.513 --> 00:38:49.265
Don't you have anything less sweet?

00:38:51.935 --> 00:38:53.686
This one is here
for a routine checkup, right?

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:54.646
MAINTENANCE HISTORY

00:38:54.729 --> 00:38:57.982
According to the maintenance history,
only the tires need replacing.

00:39:02.362 --> 00:39:03.780
Want to give it a try?

00:39:04.572 --> 00:39:05.490
No.

00:39:05.573 --> 00:39:07.492
You can learn to change a tire
in ten minutes.

00:39:07.575 --> 00:39:09.243
It's like playing with Legos.

00:39:09.327 --> 00:39:10.411
Forget it. Why would I?

00:39:12.288 --> 00:39:14.165
Do you make good money doing that?

00:39:15.166 --> 00:39:16.459
Some months are good.

00:39:16.542 --> 00:39:18.878
Other times I make less than those guys.

00:39:19.796 --> 00:39:21.756
Yeong-gil, it's getting late.
Let's wrap things up.

00:39:21.839 --> 00:39:22.799
Yes, sir.

00:39:23.299 --> 00:39:24.300
Yes, sir.

00:39:26.636 --> 00:39:28.513
You're staying for dinner, right?

00:39:28.596 --> 00:39:29.681
I'm not hungry.

00:39:31.015 --> 00:39:32.684
Then why'd you even come?

00:39:32.767 --> 00:39:34.852
I saw that you have a sofa over there.

00:39:34.936 --> 00:39:37.271
-What?
-Can I crash here for the night?

00:39:39.148 --> 00:39:41.192
-Did you two fight?
-Is that a yes or a no?

00:39:55.373 --> 00:39:56.541
Are you asleep?

00:39:56.624 --> 00:39:58.751
What? No. Why?

00:40:19.856 --> 00:40:20.898
Thank you.

00:40:24.110 --> 00:40:25.194
For what?

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:31.200
I was always so jealous
of my roommate having solo exhibitions.

00:40:32.452 --> 00:40:36.372
But you're bringing my artwork
out into the world for the first time.

00:40:40.126 --> 00:40:42.003
Thank you. I really mean it.

00:40:47.300 --> 00:40:48.342
Can I…

00:40:50.845 --> 00:40:52.472
move a little closer?

00:40:53.473 --> 00:40:54.849
What?

00:40:56.267 --> 00:40:57.518
I have something to say.

00:41:15.995 --> 00:41:17.705
How close are you getting?

00:41:18.539 --> 00:41:21.709
I'm trying to get a little braver.

00:41:23.669 --> 00:41:24.670
You know…

00:41:28.508 --> 00:41:29.634
If it…

00:41:31.636 --> 00:41:33.137
weren't for you,

00:41:35.306 --> 00:41:37.391
I couldn't have done anything.

00:41:39.894 --> 00:41:40.895
You…

00:41:42.855 --> 00:41:44.148
make me…

00:41:45.566 --> 00:41:48.820
want to become something more.

00:41:52.448 --> 00:41:55.034
And I'm grateful for that.

00:41:58.204 --> 00:41:59.330
I like that.

00:42:00.498 --> 00:42:03.167
So I hope we can

00:42:04.710 --> 00:42:06.254
keep doing this together.

00:42:27.525 --> 00:42:31.487
Then we should go to bed early.

00:42:39.162 --> 00:42:40.037
Good night.

00:42:40.788 --> 00:42:41.664
Okay.

00:42:42.290 --> 00:42:43.207
You too.

00:42:58.472 --> 00:43:00.266
TRUSTED PLACE FOR TIRES

00:43:07.481 --> 00:43:10.026
You could've just slept at my place.

00:43:10.109 --> 00:43:11.360
No, thank you.

00:43:13.696 --> 00:43:14.697
Did you cheat on her?

00:43:14.780 --> 00:43:16.324
Come on.

00:43:16.949 --> 00:43:20.077
Right, there's no way
you'd do something like that.

00:43:21.162 --> 00:43:22.288
How is Su-gyeom?

00:43:22.371 --> 00:43:24.665
I heard he was studying
to retake the CSAT.

00:43:25.833 --> 00:43:27.168
He got into Yonseo University.

00:43:27.251 --> 00:43:29.045
Seriously? Damn.

00:43:29.128 --> 00:43:31.631
He's the first in our family
to get into a prestigious university.

00:43:31.714 --> 00:43:32.924
Hey, give him a call.

00:43:33.007 --> 00:43:34.717
Let me talk to him. It's been a while.

00:43:34.800 --> 00:43:35.927
Forget it.

00:43:37.094 --> 00:43:40.514
It's been a while since you last saw
Jun and Seo-in, hasn't it?

00:43:42.975 --> 00:43:44.352
Look.

00:43:44.435 --> 00:43:46.312
The kids have grown up so much.

00:43:50.816 --> 00:43:52.777
Say something, you jerk.

00:44:04.789 --> 00:44:07.708
So did you finally become an executive?

00:44:09.085 --> 00:44:10.753
I quit.

00:44:12.838 --> 00:44:14.090
What?

00:44:17.218 --> 00:44:18.844
You worked there long enough.

00:44:23.015 --> 00:44:24.225
I was fired.

00:44:25.142 --> 00:44:26.936
I was demoted to the factory,

00:44:27.019 --> 00:44:29.814
and I kept disobeying orders,

00:44:29.897 --> 00:44:31.148
so I got kicked out.

00:44:35.194 --> 00:44:37.280
When you hear something like that,

00:44:37.363 --> 00:44:38.489
how does it make you feel?

00:44:39.699 --> 00:44:40.992
What do you mean?

00:44:41.075 --> 00:44:44.787
When you hear that I never became
an executive and got fired from my job,

00:44:44.870 --> 00:44:46.038
how does that make you feel?

00:44:48.499 --> 00:44:50.584
I'm just wondering how big
your severance package was.

00:44:50.668 --> 00:44:53.879
I got 500 million won,
but I blew it all on something stupid.

00:44:55.006 --> 00:44:58.050
So? How does that make you feel?

00:44:58.134 --> 00:44:59.927
What are you getting at?

00:45:00.011 --> 00:45:02.513
When you didn't get into
Seoul National University,

00:45:04.849 --> 00:45:06.267
I was really happy.

00:45:07.226 --> 00:45:10.354
During the IMF crisis,
when you got fired from your job,

00:45:10.438 --> 00:45:12.940
and when you ran your business
into the ground,

00:45:13.607 --> 00:45:15.401
I was honestly really happy.

00:45:16.902 --> 00:45:19.864
So? Does that change your opinion?

00:45:25.494 --> 00:45:26.829
Well, I don't know.

00:45:34.712 --> 00:45:38.174
When we were kids,
Mom once brought some bananas.

00:45:39.633 --> 00:45:40.676
Bananas?

00:45:40.760 --> 00:45:42.636
They were really expensive back then.

00:45:44.930 --> 00:45:48.893
A bunch would cost
around 100,000 won today.

00:45:50.102 --> 00:45:51.687
Mom gave me two,

00:45:52.480 --> 00:45:53.939
and she gave you three.

00:45:55.524 --> 00:45:59.236
But when I got home from school,
there was only one banana left on my desk.

00:46:00.237 --> 00:46:01.489
So I went to you

00:46:01.572 --> 00:46:04.200
and asked why there was only one left.

00:46:05.701 --> 00:46:06.827
You don't remember?

00:46:09.622 --> 00:46:10.873
What did I say?

00:46:10.956 --> 00:46:12.500
You said you didn't know.

00:46:12.583 --> 00:46:15.294
I went to your room,
dug through the trash,

00:46:15.378 --> 00:46:16.504
and found the peel.

00:46:16.587 --> 00:46:18.756
I brought it to you and started yelling,

00:46:18.839 --> 00:46:20.466
asking why you ate mine.

00:46:23.010 --> 00:46:24.637
Do you know what you did to me?

00:46:27.598 --> 00:46:29.892
You slapped me.

00:46:32.895 --> 00:46:34.814
I went crying to Mom,

00:46:36.440 --> 00:46:37.316
and she said,

00:46:37.400 --> 00:46:41.028
"So what if your brother had one more?
What's the big deal?"

00:46:41.112 --> 00:46:45.616
When I said you'd hit me,
she just stopped responding.

00:46:47.243 --> 00:46:48.244
Jeez.

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:53.207
That's what I was to the family.

00:47:07.012 --> 00:47:09.306
For the first time, in third grade,

00:47:09.974 --> 00:47:12.184
I came home so happy
about being class vice president.

00:47:12.268 --> 00:47:13.561
Remember what you said?

00:47:15.604 --> 00:47:16.605
No.

00:47:16.689 --> 00:47:18.232
You don't remember?

00:47:18.315 --> 00:47:20.401
Damn it, I said I don't know!

00:47:23.279 --> 00:47:24.572
Gosh, you…

00:47:26.031 --> 00:47:27.616
don't remember anything at all.

00:47:40.880 --> 00:47:42.882
I'm the only one who remembers.

00:47:48.512 --> 00:47:49.805
I'm turning in.

00:48:19.502 --> 00:48:22.004
The person who came yesterday
didn't like it either?

00:48:22.087 --> 00:48:25.424
I guess rent-free for three months
isn't good enough.

00:48:25.508 --> 00:48:29.178
Then please list it as available
for a short-term lease.

00:48:29.261 --> 00:48:30.971
That's probably for the best.

00:48:31.597 --> 00:48:33.057
Take your time looking around.

00:48:33.140 --> 00:48:34.391
Okay, thank you.

00:48:35.643 --> 00:48:37.686
I almost forgot. Ma'am.

00:48:37.770 --> 00:48:42.274
Please tell your husband
not to sleep here, if possible.

00:48:42.358 --> 00:48:43.275
Excuse me?

00:48:43.359 --> 00:48:45.486
It makes him look too desperate.

00:48:45.569 --> 00:48:49.240
From a potential tenant's perspective,
that's actually a major drawback.

00:48:50.449 --> 00:48:51.992
Wait, he sleeps here?

00:48:52.076 --> 00:48:55.037
Oh, so you didn't know.

00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:59.458
Well, take a look around.

00:49:05.839 --> 00:49:06.924
What is that?

00:49:07.925 --> 00:49:08.801
Gosh.

00:49:20.854 --> 00:49:22.147
URGENT SALE

00:49:22.314 --> 00:49:23.649
URGENT SALE
500M WON → 380M WON

00:49:23.732 --> 00:49:24.775
FOR LEASE

00:49:33.075 --> 00:49:34.368
FOR LEASE
THREE MILLION PER MONTH

00:49:36.453 --> 00:49:40.499
Nak-su. My dear Kim Nak-su.

00:49:42.084 --> 00:49:43.043
Jeez.

00:49:44.253 --> 00:49:45.254
Come on in.

00:49:46.463 --> 00:49:49.049
You already bought the place.
What more do you have to say?

00:49:49.133 --> 00:49:51.885
Just sit down and listen.
Su-gyeom, you too.

00:49:51.969 --> 00:49:54.013
-Gosh.
-Quick. Sit down.

00:49:54.096 --> 00:49:56.390
Okay, listen carefully.

00:49:56.890 --> 00:49:58.976
From the front door to the bathroom,

00:49:59.059 --> 00:50:01.312
and Su-gyeom, up to your room.

00:50:01.395 --> 00:50:04.189
That was ten years' salary
as an associate and assistant manager.

00:50:04.273 --> 00:50:05.274
Next.

00:50:05.357 --> 00:50:08.652
The kitchen, the utility room,
and this bedroom here.

00:50:08.736 --> 00:50:11.322
All that cost me five years
of my salary as a manager.

00:50:11.405 --> 00:50:16.452
Finally, for five years
as a senior manager,

00:50:16.535 --> 00:50:19.788
I worked my fingers to the bone
and scraped together every last penny.

00:50:20.664 --> 00:50:24.126
And with all that, we barely bought
this living room and that balcony.

00:50:24.752 --> 00:50:28.422
You kept saying
that you were sick of moving around,

00:50:28.505 --> 00:50:29.923
so I reluctantly bought it.

00:50:30.674 --> 00:50:32.843
But don't forget this, you two.

00:50:33.636 --> 00:50:34.970
This apartment

00:50:36.013 --> 00:50:38.015
is the culmination

00:50:39.725 --> 00:50:40.976
of my 51 years.

00:50:42.478 --> 00:50:43.729
My trophy.

00:50:46.982 --> 00:50:48.067
Understand?

00:50:48.150 --> 00:50:49.568
You're the best!

00:50:50.653 --> 00:50:51.904
Dad, you're the best!

00:50:54.740 --> 00:50:56.241
Bring it in.

00:50:56.325 --> 00:50:57.534
You worked hard too, honey.

00:50:57.618 --> 00:51:00.371
Good job!

00:51:02.498 --> 00:51:04.375
-This is our home!
-Let's have a drink.

00:51:05.959 --> 00:51:06.877
All right.

00:51:19.098 --> 00:51:20.683
What do we do?

00:51:21.558 --> 00:51:24.269
We can't live off the trophy.

00:52:13.944 --> 00:52:15.112
Hey, you're up.

00:52:15.612 --> 00:52:16.655
I'm leaving.

00:52:16.739 --> 00:52:17.740
Okay.

00:52:18.615 --> 00:52:19.658
I slept well.

00:52:20.284 --> 00:52:21.326
All right.

00:52:22.286 --> 00:52:23.746
-Good morning.
-Good morning, sir.

00:52:23.829 --> 00:52:25.873
You're slacking off.
You should come early.

00:52:25.956 --> 00:52:28.000
What do you mean?
We're five minutes early.

00:52:28.083 --> 00:52:29.418
-Hello, sir.
-Hello.

00:52:29.501 --> 00:52:31.003
Ask him. Go on.

00:52:31.086 --> 00:52:32.504
No, you ask him.

00:52:33.589 --> 00:52:36.300
Excuse me. Are you the boss's brother?

00:52:39.303 --> 00:52:41.388
-Man!
-Give it to me.

00:52:41.472 --> 00:52:43.098
They don't look alike at all.

00:52:43.182 --> 00:52:45.350
Look at their faces. It's obvious.

00:52:45.434 --> 00:52:47.144
You must have money to burn.

00:52:47.227 --> 00:52:48.645
Go get changed, you guys.

00:52:48.729 --> 00:52:49.605
Yes, sir.

00:52:49.688 --> 00:52:52.483
The boss talks about you all the time.

00:52:52.566 --> 00:52:53.567
What did he say?

00:52:53.650 --> 00:52:55.736
He was bragging about
how high up you were at ACT--

00:52:55.819 --> 00:52:57.988
-Hey!
-Okay, I'm going.

00:52:58.781 --> 00:53:00.866
-Come on, you're buying coffee.
-What?

00:53:00.949 --> 00:53:02.785
That guy loves to run his mouth.

00:53:02.868 --> 00:53:03.744
Go.

00:53:06.538 --> 00:53:09.291
I left something
on the desk in the office.

00:53:09.917 --> 00:53:10.959
Take it with you.

00:53:25.432 --> 00:53:28.644
I ate it. I'm sorry.

00:53:50.958 --> 00:53:54.962
What if my brother had apologized then?

00:53:55.045 --> 00:53:57.047
What if he'd just said "congratulations"

00:53:57.548 --> 00:54:00.050
when I became class vice president?

00:54:01.051 --> 00:54:02.052
Would I be different?

00:54:03.470 --> 00:54:04.555
How so?

00:54:04.638 --> 00:54:10.102
For one thing, I might not see
everyone in the world as my competitor,

00:54:11.061 --> 00:54:14.147
and I might not be as jealous

00:54:14.231 --> 00:54:15.274
and as prideful.

00:54:15.357 --> 00:54:17.693
Jeez. You can never know.

00:54:17.776 --> 00:54:20.404
Not unless we can travel
to a parallel universe.

00:54:21.655 --> 00:54:23.782
Besides, that competitiveness

00:54:23.866 --> 00:54:25.993
may have been what's kept you going

00:54:26.076 --> 00:54:28.745
and put food on the table
for your family all this time.

00:54:28.829 --> 00:54:32.082
You're right. That's true.

00:54:32.875 --> 00:54:36.003
Also, that may be what led you
to make a risky investment

00:54:36.086 --> 00:54:38.547
to prove you're not washed up yet.

00:54:41.633 --> 00:54:43.719
And my appetite is gone.

00:54:47.097 --> 00:54:49.016
How many children do you have?

00:54:50.058 --> 00:54:51.184
I've got a son.

00:54:51.268 --> 00:54:53.562
Then you must be giving your son

00:54:53.645 --> 00:54:55.731
all the love and encouragement

00:54:55.814 --> 00:54:58.150
you didn't get from your parents

00:54:59.192 --> 00:55:00.736
when you were young.

00:55:02.321 --> 00:55:04.489
-Well…
-And you must express your love a lot.

00:55:07.284 --> 00:55:11.204
I may have failed at other things,
but when it comes to him,

00:55:11.288 --> 00:55:15.042
I've been making sure
he gets the best education available.

00:55:16.001 --> 00:55:18.795
I had him attend the best academies

00:55:18.879 --> 00:55:20.631
and got him private tutoring too.

00:55:20.714 --> 00:55:22.341
I've really gone all out.

00:55:24.801 --> 00:55:27.095
Do you know how that sounds to me?

00:55:29.765 --> 00:55:33.101
"I bought him all the bananas
I couldn't have as a child."

00:55:34.144 --> 00:55:35.270
That's how it sounds.

00:55:35.896 --> 00:55:37.731
Except nowadays,

00:55:37.814 --> 00:55:41.109
these bananas only cost 3,000 won a bunch.

00:56:02.881 --> 00:56:03.757
Honey.

00:56:09.179 --> 00:56:10.055
Honey?

00:56:23.235 --> 00:56:24.403
Let's see.

00:56:25.612 --> 00:56:27.364
What did she make today?

00:56:52.347 --> 00:56:53.682
Should I make another one?

00:56:56.101 --> 00:56:57.102
No.

00:56:57.185 --> 00:57:00.188
If she leaves work early,
your mom gets home around six o'clock.

00:57:00.272 --> 00:57:01.857
Want some?

00:57:01.940 --> 00:57:03.650
No, you can have it, Dad.

00:57:10.824 --> 00:57:12.117
Where are you staying?

00:57:12.868 --> 00:57:16.038
Mostly at internet cafes
or my friend's place.

00:57:17.748 --> 00:57:18.665
Okay.

00:57:25.630 --> 00:57:26.631
Hey.

00:57:28.550 --> 00:57:32.137
Did you really not want
to retake the CSAT?

00:57:39.436 --> 00:57:40.854
It was my decision.

00:57:48.904 --> 00:57:50.405
Should we add some rice?

00:57:51.073 --> 00:57:52.074
No.

00:57:52.657 --> 00:57:54.534
-Mom gets here at six--
-It won't take long.

00:57:54.618 --> 00:57:55.619
No, we can't, Dad.

00:57:59.456 --> 00:58:00.999
What is it?

00:58:04.336 --> 00:58:05.754
What did I tell you?

00:58:05.837 --> 00:58:07.672
Good thing we didn't make more ramyeon.

00:58:08.340 --> 00:58:11.551
Good things happen when you listen
to your old man. You hear me?

00:58:12.886 --> 00:58:15.055
You wanted to add rice. And I stopped you.

00:58:15.138 --> 00:58:17.265
You little rascal.

00:58:27.734 --> 00:58:29.319
Did she go in?

00:58:29.402 --> 00:58:30.737
Be careful.

00:58:33.740 --> 00:58:34.741
Did she go up?

00:58:37.828 --> 00:58:39.538
She's gone.

00:58:52.008 --> 00:58:54.261
-Working as a designated driver again?
-Yes.

00:58:55.220 --> 00:58:57.264
-What? Are you ashamed of me?
-No.

00:58:57.347 --> 00:58:59.558
Why would I be ashamed of you for working?

00:59:02.435 --> 00:59:05.480
I'm just worried
you'll get into an accident.

00:59:07.065 --> 00:59:08.275
I won't, kid.

00:59:09.276 --> 00:59:11.945
That only happened
because some guy was acting crazy.

00:59:12.028 --> 00:59:14.114
I'll be careful, don't worry.

00:59:14.197 --> 00:59:15.407
Go on inside.

00:59:16.908 --> 00:59:18.535
Actually…

00:59:20.996 --> 00:59:22.998
Do you want to work together?

00:59:25.041 --> 00:59:26.084
Why do you want to?

00:59:26.751 --> 00:59:29.838
What do you mean, "Why?"
I have a 30 million won debt to pay.

00:59:31.214 --> 00:59:32.340
Jeez.

00:59:42.642 --> 00:59:45.145
Are you okay with going
to Pyeongtaek at this hour?

00:59:45.228 --> 00:59:46.730
How are you going to get back?

00:59:47.480 --> 00:59:48.857
I'll be fine, sir.

01:00:15.300 --> 01:00:16.635
Here's your key.

01:00:16.718 --> 01:00:18.470
-Thanks for driving.
-Yes, thank you.

01:00:25.018 --> 01:00:25.977
All right.

01:00:26.603 --> 01:00:27.562
Welcome back.

01:00:32.609 --> 01:00:33.902
AWAITING RIDE REQUEST

01:00:33.985 --> 01:00:34.903
We got one!

01:00:34.986 --> 01:00:37.489
-Where is it?
-It's a ride to Suwon.

01:00:37.572 --> 01:00:38.448
CALL CUSTOMER

01:00:38.531 --> 01:00:40.033
Let's go.

01:01:19.864 --> 01:01:21.032
-Here.
-Thank you.

01:01:21.116 --> 01:01:22.200
Hold on.

01:01:22.826 --> 01:01:24.035
Here's your tip.

01:01:24.119 --> 01:01:25.745
-Thank you, sir.
-Sure.

01:01:25.829 --> 01:01:27.163
-Thank you too.
-Su-gyeom!

01:01:31.918 --> 01:01:34.212
Look! I got a tip.

01:01:42.887 --> 01:01:44.055
Why is this so delicious?

01:01:44.139 --> 01:01:46.391
It even has egg in it.

01:01:46.474 --> 01:01:48.727
Go easy, Dad. Or you'll get a stomachache.

01:01:50.687 --> 01:01:51.771
Aren't you tired?

01:01:53.189 --> 01:01:54.232
No, I'm fine.

01:01:54.316 --> 01:01:55.859
Well, your dad is tired.

01:01:58.111 --> 01:01:59.029
And cold.

01:02:00.572 --> 01:02:01.740
Dad, are you cold?

01:02:02.240 --> 01:02:03.658
If you are…

01:02:07.203 --> 01:02:08.330
AWAITING RIDE REQUEST

01:02:08.621 --> 01:02:10.206
-We got one. Let's go.
-We got it.

01:02:10.290 --> 01:02:11.458
Come on. Let's go.

01:02:50.705 --> 01:02:52.999
Oh, my legs. Jeez.

01:03:17.023 --> 01:03:17.982
WITHDRAWABLE EARNINGS

01:03:18.066 --> 01:03:20.360
We made 340,000 won, Dad.

01:03:20.443 --> 01:03:22.779
Is it because we accepted
long-distance requests?

01:03:22.862 --> 01:03:26.157
After 40,000 won for gas,
that leaves us with 300,000 won.

01:03:26.241 --> 01:03:28.076
-Yes.
-Gosh.

01:03:28.159 --> 01:03:30.245
I get 160,000 won,
and you get 140,000 won.

01:03:30.328 --> 01:03:31.579
Why?

01:03:31.663 --> 01:03:32.997
Your hoodie's 10,000 won.

01:03:33.081 --> 01:03:34.374
You're ruthless.

01:03:34.958 --> 01:03:36.251
Jeez.

01:03:36.751 --> 01:03:38.378
How many of these did you sell?

01:03:40.630 --> 01:03:42.590
-About a hundred.
-A hundred?

01:03:43.299 --> 01:03:45.093
That's more than I expected.

01:03:45.176 --> 01:03:46.261
No, it's nothing.

01:03:46.344 --> 01:03:48.388
You're better than me, son.

01:03:48.471 --> 01:03:51.349
My commercial unit
has been empty for three months.

01:03:52.392 --> 01:03:54.102
Finally, I can pat your head.

01:03:55.520 --> 01:03:57.730
So, are you going to keep doing it?

01:03:59.065 --> 01:04:00.024
I have to.

01:04:01.443 --> 01:04:02.318
Good.

01:04:02.986 --> 01:04:05.071
That's what business is all about.

01:04:05.864 --> 01:04:08.658
Sometimes it's good,
and sometimes it's bad.

01:04:09.367 --> 01:04:13.580
The market trends are really subtle.

01:04:13.663 --> 01:04:17.167
That's why you always have to listen
to what people are saying.

01:04:17.250 --> 01:04:21.004
You know, the ladies at restaurants
and the taxi drivers.

01:04:21.087 --> 01:04:23.423
That's where you find the market trends.

01:04:25.300 --> 01:04:27.844
You're missing some expensive consulting.

01:04:31.973 --> 01:04:34.392
Fine. Get some sleep.

01:04:37.770 --> 01:04:38.897
You must be exhausted.

01:04:43.485 --> 01:04:45.445
But your dad is not.

01:05:25.235 --> 01:05:27.695
They just waltz in whenever they please.

01:05:29.739 --> 01:05:30.823
Fine.

01:05:52.554 --> 01:05:53.471
Gosh.

01:06:19.747 --> 01:06:21.082
My Su-gyeom.

01:07:22.977 --> 01:07:25.229
HOME PHOTOS
OPEN

01:07:25.396 --> 01:07:27.357
JIKHOME
UPLOAD PHOTOS

01:07:27.732 --> 01:07:28.691
LIST PROPERTY

01:07:38.076 --> 01:07:41.287
DO YOU WANT TO LIST THIS PROPERTY?

01:08:01.974 --> 01:08:03.142
LIST IT

01:08:05.895 --> 01:08:08.856
LISTING COMPLETED

01:08:31.170 --> 01:08:35.508
THE DREAM LIFE OF MR. KIM

01:09:05.663 --> 01:09:07.248
I told you I'm not selling the apartment.

01:09:07.331 --> 01:09:08.583
Why don't you do this for real?

01:09:09.500 --> 01:09:12.837
Do you really think I could handle
living in a place like that?

01:09:12.920 --> 01:09:14.839
You're on your way
to see the president, right?

01:09:14.922 --> 01:09:19.093
Do Jin-woo betrayed me and sided with
Executive Director Hwang Tae-san.

01:09:19.635 --> 01:09:22.722
We're sick and tired
of being treated like we're invisible.

01:09:23.765 --> 01:09:25.308
Hey, Nak-su.

01:09:25.933 --> 01:09:27.727
So please just help me one last time.

01:09:27.810 --> 01:09:29.687
It must be a job where you're needed.

01:09:29.771 --> 01:09:31.647
Something only you can do.

01:09:32.482 --> 01:09:34.233
Managing Director Kim Nak-su.

01:09:35.818 --> 01:09:37.818
Subtitle translation by Soya Back